# Next.js Pages & Booking Flow

## App Router
- Pages live in `app/**/page.tsx`. Layouts in `layout.tsx`.
- Client components: add `'use client'` at top when using useState, useEffect, or event handlers.
- Navigation: `useRouter()` from `next/navigation`; `router.push(path)`.

## Booking Flow (Order)
1. `app/booking/location/page.tsx` – Choose location; store in sessionStorage as `bookingLocation`.
2. `app/booking/date-time/page.tsx` – Requires `bookingLocation`; fetches slots by locationId; stores `bookingDateTime`.
3. `app/booking/customer/page.tsx` – Requires location + dateTime; stores `customerDetails`.
4. `app/booking/services/page.tsx` – Requires location, dateTime, customer; can preload `selectedServices` from sessionStorage; stores for payment.
5. `app/booking/payment/page.tsx` – Creates booking via POST `/api/booking` with locationId and services; then redirects to confirmation.
Redirect to `/booking/location` if required sessionStorage keys are missing.

## Admin
- Dashboard: `app/admin/page.tsx`. Sub-routes: bookings, reports, customize, locations, categories.
- Customize: hero videos (max 5, MP4, max 30s), gallery images, locations link. No UI text about “R2” or storage.
- Locations: max 2; edit name, address, mobile, imageUrl. Back link goes to `/admin/customize`.
- Reports: location filter, period (day/week/month/year), date; shows summary and bookings list.

## Conventions
- Use Tailwind; prefer responsive classes (`sm:`, `md:`). Touch targets min 44px where possible.
- ServiceCard: accept `isSelected` to show “Already selected” and disable add.
- Images: use placeholder until load (e.g. `lib/placeholders.ts`) to avoid blank flash.
